<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <GenerateProgramFile>false</GenerateProgramFile>

    <!-- Package Metadata -->
    <Version>1.5.0</Version>
    <PackageId>FSharp.Azure.Quantum</PackageId>
    <Title>FSharp.Azure.Quantum</Title>
    <Description>F# library for Azure Quantum with quantum-first optimization (Graph Coloring, TSP, MaxCut, Knapsack, Network Flow, Portfolio), Azure Quantum backend integration (IonQ, Rigetti, Quantinuum, Atom Computing), extensible circuit validation, local quantum simulation, QAOA with automatic parameter optimization (Nelder-Mead), OpenQASM 2.0 support, error mitigation techniques (ZNE, PEC, REM), Quantum Random Number Generation (QRNG), and educational quantum algorithms (Grover, QFT, Amplitude Amplification, QPE, Shor, HHL) and quantum chemistry (VQE, QPE) with cloud backend execution as whole-circuit jobs. Native IQuantumBackend integration for IonQ, Rigetti, Quantinuum, Atom Computing, IQM and D-Wave, plus Pasqal neutral-atom analog hardware (via Pulser) and a neutral-atom analog programming model; additional platforms (IBM, Amazon Braket, Google Cirq) are targetable via OpenQASM 2.0 export/import.</Description>
    <Summary>F# library for Azure Quantum with quantum-first optimization, quantum backends (IonQ, Rigetti, Quantinuum, Atom Computing), QAOA with automatic parameter tuning, QRNG, and educational algorithms with cloud execution</Summary>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v1.5.0: Task-based API; no Azure Quantum SDK dependency
- BREAKING: every solver, builder, ML and algorithm entry point is `xAsync … cancellationToken : Task&lt;…&gt;`; the synchronous and Async&lt;_&gt; variants and all [&lt;Obsolete&gt;] wrappers are gone. Migrate `X.solve …` → `X.solveAsync … CancellationToken.None`; in a script finish with `|&gt; Async.AwaitTask |&gt; Async.RunSynchronously`
- BREAKING: every computation expression (`binaryClassification`, `optionPricing`, `chemistry`, …) returns Task&lt;QuantumResult&lt;_&gt;&gt;; the C# builders expose only `…Async(…, CancellationToken)`
- BREAKING (workspace): AzureQuantumWorkspace reads quotas and provider status from the REST data plane; Microsoft.Azure.Quantum.Client and Azure.Quantum.Jobs are no longer referenced. WorkspaceConfig gains HttpClient (and createWithHttpClient); InnerWorkspace is gone
- CHANGED (cloud fan-out): kernel matrices, SVM evaluation, VQC and Primitives.sampleBatchAsync/observeBatchAsync keep at most JobThrottle.MaxConcurrentSampledJobs (8) circuits in flight on a sampling backend; error-mitigation noise levels and benchmark suites run one after another
- CHANGED: cancellation surfaces as OperationCanceledException instead of an Error; Knapsack's classical fallback no longer runs after the caller cancelled
- CHANGED (bin packing): the bin bound is the first-fit-decreasing count, not the item count, so a 6-item problem that fits 2 bins takes 14 qubits instead of 42
- CHANGED (cost dashboard): "today" and "this month" buckets use the local calendar instead of UTC
- ADDED (LocalQuantumService): GET {workspace}/quotas and GET {workspace}/providerStatus, so the workspace client runs offline too
- FIXED (tests): the QuantumClient facts returned Async&lt;unit&gt; and were never run by xUnit; they run now
</PackageReleaseNotes>

